    "name": "rowan",
    "notes": "THE BERRIES ARE THE SPECIES AND THERE IS NO FRUIT PRIMITIVE. What the generator has is a leaf material, so the crown is drawn in `leaf_autumn` -- the orange -- at a low density with wide separation, which reads as an open airy crown loaded with orange rather than as an autumn tree. That is a deliberate substitution and the honest way to get a berry tree at 10 cm; a fruit pass would be the real fix and would serve the crab apple, the hawthorn and the sea buckthorn too.\n\nSmall, upright and slim, so it fits under a canopy edge.",
